<title>MEXICO: Pemex announces two successful well tests.</title>
<headline>Pemex announces two successful well tests.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>State oil monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said Thursday two successful well tests confirmed major extensions to hydrocarbon deposits.</p>
<p>Pemex said in a statement the Manik-1 underwater well in the Campeche Sound tested 7,500 bpd of oil and six million cfd of natural gas. And the Arcos-505 well in Tampico showed a production capacity of more than 15 million cfd of natgas.</p>
</text>
